{
  "note": [
    "Physical Plant Two's fabric, cut from the one Lawanda layout in scripts/fabric-lawanda.mjs -- regenerate from there, do not hand-edit. PHYSICAL-PLANT-TWO v3 with the 2026-09-17 geometry pass: 20 x 10 x 24, the eye at the middle -- deliberately much larger than the Kalamontee plant. A clear aisle runs east from the mouth, air handlers stand either side of it and along the walls, ducts and pipe runs cross overhead, and the ceiling is 10 m up.",
    "One opening, west, and it is THE BIG MOUTH: 4.5 x 3.6 against the 1.8 x 2.6 of the small doorways, which is the room description's point about this plant. The eye is 10 m from it and Systems Corridor East beyond is 3.8 m high and 12 m long, so its whole section stands inside the opening -- deck-plate floor, worn concrete walls, its ceiling from 11 m out.",
    "This is the east end of the 45 m line the whole cluster is built around, read backwards. At 22.16 m the corridor's own 2.2 x 2.6 west mouth, through it SYSTEMS-CORRIDOR, then that corridor's west mouth at 34.32 m, and at last a strip of SYSTEMS-CORRIDOR-WEST's west wall 44.48 m from the eye: about 2.9 m of wall, floor to 2.90 m up, 1.43 m each side of the axis. WHAT IS NOT IN IT, and a reader will expect them: the corridor's north and south doorways to Course Control and the Library Lobby are 5 m off this axis 16.16 m out where the cone reaches 3.64 m, SO NEITHER SHOWS, and neither room is in the scene; the Infirmary's mouth and the walk to the Fork are round the bend past the far end and never show; and Systems Corridor's CEILING does not show either -- past the second mouth the up-slope is 0.045, which reaches 3.15 m at 34.32 m against a 3.6 m ceiling. The hallway is warm-lit from its own strips and reads dimmer, lower and much smaller than this hall. No door leaf anywhere along it."
  ],
